From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] venus: host image copies for single-plane formats only

ffmpeg's Vulkan filters hung on uploaded frames: its hwupload fills
images with VK_EXT_host_image_copy, and a 3-plane yuv420p image filled
that way hung the host GPU at its first use on a queue (NVIDIA: Xid 109,
context switch timeout), while frames the GPU decoded, 2-plane NV12
uploads and single-plane images (disable_multiplane=1) all work. The
2-plane formats already lose VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_2_HOST_IMAGE_TRANSFER_BIT
to the 32-bit YCbCr feature mask; now every multi-planar format does, so
applications upload those through a buffer on the GPU. The fault in the
multi-planar host copy path itself isn't found.

Also: a host copy region of one plane is sized with the plane's format
(vk_format_get_aspect_format), not the image's.
---
diff --git a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_host_copy.c b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_host_copy.c
index 7a294a3..6714103 100644
--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_host_copy.c
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_host_copy.c
@@ -128,6 +128,13 @@ vn_get_copy_size(VkImage img_handle,
    else if (!copy_depth && copy_stencil)
       format = vk_format_stencil_only(format);
 
+   /* A plane of a multi-planar image: the plane's own format (its texel size; the region's extent is in the plane's
+    * texels). The image's format gave chroma planes the wrong size, and the host copied from past the data sent */
+   const VkImageAspectFlags plane_aspects =
+      VK_IMAGE_ASPECT_PLANE_0_BIT | VK_IMAGE_ASPECT_PLANE_1_BIT | VK_IMAGE_ASPECT_PLANE_2_BIT;
+   if (subres_layers->aspectMask & plane_aspects)
+      format = vk_format_get_aspect_format(format, subres_layers->aspectMask & plane_aspects);
+
    const uint32_t width = mem_row_length ?: img_extent.width;
    const uint32_t height = mem_img_height ?: img_extent.height;
    const uint32_t bw = vk_format_get_blockwidth(format);
diff --git a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_physical_device.c b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_physical_device.c
index 0bc2177..7a6b543 100644
--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_physical_device.c
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
 #include "venus-protocol/vn_protocol_driver_device.h"
 #include "vk_android.h"
 #include "vk_common_entrypoints.h"
+#include "vk_format.h"
 
 #include "vn_android.h"
 #include "vn_instance.h"
@@ -2200,6 +2201,16 @@ vn_sanitize_format_properties(VkFormat format,
    default:
       break;
    }
+
+   /* Host image copies (VK_EXT_host_image_copy) only for single-plane formats: a 3-plane image filled by host copies
+    * hung the host GPU at its first use on a queue (NVIDIA: Xid 109; ffmpeg's yuv420p uploads before any Vulkan
+    * filter), the 2-plane formats above already lose the bit to the 32-bit mask, and single-plane images (ffmpeg with
+    * disable_multiplane=1) work. Without the bit applications upload through a buffer on the GPU. ponytail: the fault
+    * in the multi-planar host copy path isn't found */
+   if (props3 && vk_format_get_plane_count(format) > 1) {
+      props3->linearTilingFeatures &= ~VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_2_HOST_IMAGE_TRANSFER_BIT;
+      props3->optimalTilingFeatures &= ~VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_2_HOST_IMAGE_TRANSFER_BIT;
+   }
 }
 
 VKAPI_ATTR void VKAPI_CALL
